---How loud a control is; success confirms what just happened (Copied).
---@alias kit.Variant "default"|"primary"|"ghost"|"danger"|"success"

---What a badge, a stat or a toast is about.
---@alias kit.Tone "neutral"|"info"|"accent"|"ok"|"warn"|"danger"

---Where a cell's content sits.
---@alias kit.Align "start"|"center"|"end"

---Which way a split divides.
---@alias kit.Axis "row"|"column"

---The look: Ledger's paper and ink, Phosphor's terminal, or Neutral's quiet
---chrome.
---@alias kit.Skin "ledger"|"phosphor"|"neutral"

---Row and control heights: 22 and 26 px, or 20 and 22 px compact.
---@alias kit.Density "comfortable"|"compact"

---A log line's level.
---@alias kit.Level "debug"|"info"|"warn"|"error"

---What a field's Choose… button asks the system for: a folder, a file to
---open, or where to save one.
---@alias kit.Browse "folder"|"open"|"save"

---How a chart labels its x axis: the number (with `x_unit`), time counted
---back to now (`-15` … `0` reads `15 min ago` … `now`), or Unix seconds
---as the local time of day.
---@alias kit.XFormat "number"|"ago"|"clock"

---Which half of the skin's colours: the OS's, or light or dark held.
---@alias kit.Appearance "system"|"light"|"dark"

---One of Kit's shaders: a skeleton's shimmer, or gradient noise.
---@alias kit.ShaderPreset "shimmer"|"noise"

---What a list or a table selects: one row, any rows (⌘- or Ctrl-click
---toggles a row, Shift extends from the last row clicked, ⌘A or Ctrl+A
---takes them all, Space toggles the row the keyboard is on), or none — the
---rows still a keyboard's to walk and Enter's to activate.
---@alias kit.Selection "single"|"multiple"|"none"

---What a skeleton stands in for: lines of text, a block (an image, a chart),
---or a circle (an avatar).
---@alias kit.SkeletonShape "text"|"block"|"circle"

---A choice: what it is, and what it reads as.
---@class kit.Choice
---@field value string What the choice is; what the event carries.
---@field label string What it reads as.
---@field disabled? boolean Shown, not choosable.
---@field count? integer A count beside the label (a segment's, a tab's).
---@field alert? boolean The count is bad news: drawn in the danger colour.

---A table's column: which field of the channel it shows, and how.
---@class kit.Column
---@field field string The channel column it reads.
---@field title string Its header.
---@field width? number Its width in px; shares the rest when left out.
---@field min_width? number How narrow a sharing column goes before the table hides a column or scrolls sideways (80 when left out).
---@field priority? number How much it matters when the table is narrow: the columns that do not fit hide lowest first, the header with them; left out, it never hides. What still does not fit scrolls sideways.
---@field align? kit.Align Where its cells sit; numbers read best at the end.
---@field mono? boolean Its cells in the data face: ids, timings, hashes.
---@field tone? string A channel column naming each cell's tone (`ok`, `warn`, `danger`, `accent`, `neutral`): the cell is drawn in it — a status, an HTTP method.
---@field badge? boolean Its cells as pills with a dot in their `tone`: a status column.

---A tab: its value and its label.
